msgstr "显示活动的卷"

#: temp.glade:27728
msgid "Select this option to only display the pictures from the\n"
"books that are currently in focus to be printed. \n"
"When unchecked, then the list will show pictures from\n"
"ALL the books in the project that have been added to\n"
"the PicList. If pictures of a certain book are missing, \n"
"then you may need to select that book and Generate\n"
"the PicList details just for *that* book."
msgstr "选择此选项可只显示当前要打印的卷中的图片。\n"
"取消选中时，列表将显示项目中已添加到\n"
"PicList 的所有卷的图片。如果缺少某一卷的图片，\n"
"可能需要选择该卷，并仅为该卷生成 PicList 详情。"

#: temp.glade:27756
msgid "Image"
msgstr "图片"

#: temp.glade:27761
msgid "Display the picture currently in focus.\n"
"Note that this is dependent on the image\n"
"being located in the specified folder(s)."
msgstr "显示当前正在查看的图片。\n"
"请注意，这取决于图像\n"
"是否位于指定的文件夹中。"

#: temp.glade:27778
msgid "Position"
msgstr "位置"

#: temp.glade:27783
msgid "Show the relative position of the picture\n"
"on the page. When Inner/Outer is used,\n"
"the position displayed represents the \n"
"odd/right-hand page of a spread."
msgstr "显示图片在页面上的相对位置。\n"
"使用内侧/外侧时，\n"
"所显示的位置代表对开页中的\n"
"奇数页（右页）。"

#: temp.glade:27880
msgid "High Resolution\n"
"(Larger File)"
msgstr "高分辨率\n"
"（文件较大）"

#: temp.glade:27909
msgid "Low Resolution\n"
"(Smaller File)"
msgstr "低分辨率\n"
"（文件较小）"

#: temp.glade:27915
msgid "Paratext stores low resolution .JPG versions of\n"
"illustrations in the project's \"Figures\" folder. If\n"
"these are used, the file size of the resulting PDF\n"
"will be relatively small, and therefore easy to\n"
"share, but the image quality will be low."
msgstr "Paratext 将低分辨率的 .JPG 版本\n"
"插图存储在项目的 \"Figures\" 文件夹中。如果使用\n"
"这些图片，生成的 PDF 文件相对较小，因此容易\n"
"分享，但图像质量较低。"

#: temp.glade:27934
msgid "Use Place-holders\n"
"(Smallest PDF File)"
msgstr "使用占位符\n"
"（最小的 PDF 文件）"

#: temp.glade:27940
msgid "Use this option to include an empty box wherever\n"
"illustrations would be placed in the final PDF. \n"
"\n"
"WHY would someone want to do this?\n"
"It is sometimes necessary to generate the smallest\n"
"possible PDF file (usually in order to send by\n"
"e-mail) or to produce a PDF to be printed\n"
"without illustrations."
msgstr "选择此选项后，最终的PDF中本应放置\n"
"插图的位置将显示一个空框。\n"
"\n"
"为什么要这样做？\n"
"有时需要生成尽可能小的\n"
"PDF文件（通常是为了通过\n"
"电子邮件发送），或生成不含插图\n"
"的PDF供打印。"

#: temp.glade:27964 temp.glade:27965
msgid "Omit Pictures Only Meant for Web or App"
msgstr "省略仅适用于网页或应用程序的图片"

#: temp.glade:27969
msgid "Only allow illustrations with the 'P'rint attribute.\n"
"\n"
"If the illustrations have been marked up with\n"
"the w/a/p notation, then it is easy to exclude\n"
"any illustrations that do not have the 'p'\n"
"attribute.  Note: w= web, a=app, p=print."
msgstr "只允许带有'P'rint属性的插图。\n"
"\n"
"如果插图已用w/a/p符号标记，\n"
"就可以轻松排除\n"
"不带'p'属性的插图。\n"
"注：w=网页，a=应用程序，p=打印。"

#: temp.glade:27989
msgid "How?"
msgstr "如何处理？"

#: temp.glade:28018 temp.glade:28019
msgid "Omit Captions "
msgstr "省略说明 "

#: temp.glade:28023
msgid "If you want to suppress the picture\n"
"captions from being displayed below\n"
"the picture, then check this option."
msgstr "如果不想在图片下方\n"
"显示图片说明，\n"
"请选中此选项。"

#: temp.glade:28040
msgid "Omit References (ch:vs)"
msgstr "省略引用（章:节）"

#: temp.glade:28044
msgid "If you only want to suppress the \n"
"reference part of the caption,\n"
"then check this option. Note that\n"
"it is not possible to just have the\n"
"references without the captions."
msgstr "如果只想隐藏图片说明中的\n"
"引用部分，请选中此选项。\n"
"注意，不能只显示引用\n"
"而不显示图片说明。"

#: temp.glade:28070
msgid "Omit Missing Pictures ..."
msgstr "省略缺失的图片..."

#: temp.glade:28075
msgid "Rather than aborting the PDF export process, pre-process\n"
"the list of illustrations and skip/ignore/remove any which\n"
"are not found in the specified location of image files.\n"
"\n"
"If Pictures are missing after preparing a PDF, then\n"
"they will be listed in the section below."
msgstr "不中止PDF输出过程，而是预先处理\n"
"插图列表，跳过/忽略/删除在指定的图片文件位置\n"
"中找不到的插图。\n"
"\n"
"如果准备PDF后仍有图片缺失，\n"
"这些图片将列在下面的部分。"

#: lib/ptxprint/runjob.py:1194 temp.glade:28097
msgid "(0 Missing)"
msgstr "（缺少 0 项）"

#: temp.glade:28108
msgid "Remove Image Borders"
msgstr "去除图像边框"

#: temp.glade:28113
msgid "Some images have a thin line on\n"
"one or more of the edges of the\n"
"picture. Enable this option to\n"
"automatically crop these unwanted\n"
"lines from the edge of pictures.\n"
"Note that this setting affects ALL\n"
"images, not just those with lines."
msgstr "一些图像在一个或多个边缘\n"
"有一条细线。\n"
"启用此选项可自动裁剪\n"
"图片边缘这些多余的线条。\n"
"请注意，此设置会影响所有\n"
"图像，而不仅仅是有线条的图像。"

#: temp.glade:28158
msgid "Get Permission..."
msgstr "申请许可..."

#: temp.glade:28164
msgid "If you are publishing (i.e. more than 50 copies) any\n"
"material with illustrations that require prior permission\n"
"to be obtained before publishing, then click this button\n"
"to automatically fill in the form requesting permission.\n"
"\n"
"Note that any missing information will need to be\n"
"filled in on the Peripherals tab before the form can\n"
"be submitted.\n"
"\n"
"After filling in any remaining details, you will need to\n"
"submit the Google form and wait for a response."
msgstr "如果要出版（即超过 50 份）任何带有插图的资料，\n"
"而这些插图需要在出版前事先获得许可，\n"
"请单击此按钮，\n"
"自动填写申请许可的表格。\n"
"\n"
"请注意，提交表格之前，需要在“外围”选项卡上\n"
"填写所有缺失的信息。\n"
"\n"
"填写完其余信息后，需要\n"
"提交 Google 表单并等待回复。"

#: temp.glade:28193
msgid "Use Other\n"
"Location: "
msgstr "使用其他\n"
"位置： "

#: temp.glade:28222
msgid "Picture Folder..."
msgstr "图片文件夹..."

#: temp.glade:28228
msgid "Select another folder which contains pictures.\n"
"PTXprint will also scan the selected folder \n"
"(and all its sub-folders) looking for all the\n"
"required illustrations in the Picture List."
msgstr "选择另一个包含图片的文件夹。\n"
"PTXprint 还会扫描所选文件夹\n"
"（及其所有子文件夹），在图片列表中查找所有\n"
"所需的插图。"

#: temp.glade:28262
msgid "Exclude\n"
"Subfolders"
msgstr "排除\n"
"子文件夹"

#: temp.glade:28268
msgid "PTXprint normally searches all the sub-folders of the\n"
"specified folder locations for the pictures it needs.\n"
"\n"
"If you would prefer that it only searches in the folder\n"
"specified directly (and NOT look in any subfolders)\n"
"then select this option. This should speed up searches\n"
"for images, but may result in some images not being\n"
"found at all."
msgstr "PTXprint 通常会在指定文件夹位置的所有子文件夹中\n"
"搜索所需的图片。\n"
"\n"
"如果只想在直接指定的文件夹中搜索\n"
"（而不在任何子文件夹中搜索），\n"
"请选择此选项。这样可以加快\n"
"图片搜索速度，但可能导致某些图片\n"
"根本找不到。"

#: temp.glade:28305
msgid "You can specify your preference for which kinds\n"
"of images are used. PTXprint will search multiple\n"
"locations for any matching images, and use the\n"
"one that best matches your preferences (if found).\n"
"\n"
"If the box is left empty, it will default to the \n"
"following search sequences:\n"
"   jpg > png > tif > bmp > pdf   - for smallest file size\n"
"or\n"
"   tif > png > jpg > bmp > pdf   - for largest file size"
msgstr "可以指定优先使用哪些类型的图像。PTXprint 会在多个\n"
"位置搜索匹配的图像，并使用最符合偏好的\n"
"图像（如果找到）。\n"
"\n"
"如果该框留空，将默认使用\n"
"以下搜索顺序：\n"
"   jpg > png > tif > bmp > pdf   - 文件最小\n"
"或\n"
"   tif > png > jpg > bmp > pdf   - 文件最大"

#: temp.glade:28317
msgid "Image Types:"
msgstr "图像类型："

#: temp.glade:28331
msgid "If multiple versions of an image are located\n"
"(hk12345B.jpg, hk12345C.png or hk12345B.tif)\n"
"then which one of these different image types\n"
"should be used in the publication?\n"
"\n"
"If in doubt, leave this box empty. Then it will\n"
"use one of two defaults:\n"
"\n"
"1. Low Resolution Default Order:\n"
"JPG PNG TIF BMP PDF  (use JPGs first, if none then PNGs, TIFs etc.)\n"
"\n"
"2. High Resolution Default Order:\n"
"TIF PNG JPG BMP PDF (use TIFs first, if none then PNGs, JPGs etc.)\n"
"\n"
"Or manually type in a custom order, for example:\n"
"PDF TIF PNG (use PDFs first, otherwise TIFs, or PNGs)\n"
"  or\n"
"JPG  (only use JPGs - ignore all other file types)\n"
"  or\n"
"TIF  (only use TIFs - ignore all other file types)\n"
"\n"
"NOTE: TIF files are converted internally to hi-res JPGs."
msgstr "如果找到同一图像的多个版本\n"
"（hk12345B.jpg、hk12345C.png 或 hk12345B.tif），\n"
"出版物中应使用哪种图像类型？\n"
"\n"
"如有疑问，请将此框留空，\n"
"将使用以下两种默认顺序之一：\n"
"\n"
"1. 低分辨率默认顺序：\n"
"JPG PNG TIF BMP PDF （先用 JPG，没有则用 PNG、TIF 等）\n"
"\n"
"2. 高分辨率默认顺序：\n"
"TIF PNG JPG BMP PDF （先用 TIF，没有则用 PNG、JPG 等）\n"
"\n"
"也可以手动输入自定义顺序，例如：\n"
"PDF TIF PNG （先用 PDF，否则用 TIF 或 PNG）\n"
"  或\n"
"JPG  （仅使用 JPG，忽略其他所有文件类型）\n"
"  或\n"
"TIF  （仅使用 TIF，忽略其他所有文件类型）\n"
"\n"
"注：TIF 文件会在内部转换为高分辨率 JPG。"

#: temp.glade:28375 temp.glade:28376
msgid "Include Pictures (illustrations)"
msgstr "包含图片（插图）"

#: temp.glade:28441
msgid "Overview of the Pictures used in the publication."
msgstr "出版物中使用的图片概览。"

#: temp.glade:28442
msgid "Global Options"
msgstr "全局选项"

#: temp.glade:28486 temp.glade:28514
msgid "The anchor specifies what page in a book a picture will appear on. It appears on the same page as its anchor in the text. You can alter the Anchor Ref by a few verses to change the page on which it appears.\n"
"\n"
"An Anchor Ref must consist of a book code, perhaps followed by L or R (in the case of a diglot), then a space, then an in-book location which contains a dot (period). In a scripture book, the in-book location is Chap.Verse where the Verse matches the \\v value precisely. In other books, the in-book location can be anything as long as it is unique in that book and contains a dot (period).\n"
"\n"
"Anchor Refs for Diglots use the L or R suffix on the 3-letter book code to indicate whether the picture is to be associated with the Primary (L) text or the Secondary (R) text.\n"
"\n"
"In the glossary book (GLO) there is special support for \\k Keywords\\k* where in-book location of k.keyword(s) will anchor a picture to the corresponding term. The in-book location must match the value of the \\k Keyword or phrase\\k* with its spaces removed. For example,\n"
"\n"
"    GLO k.Altar - would link it to \\k Altar\\k*\n"
"    GLO k.JohntheBaptist - would link a picture to\n"
"               a glossary entry \\k John the Baptist\\k*\n"
"\n"
"You can copy-and-paste a glossary word or phrase after typing GLO k. and PTXprint will automatically strip the spaces for you.\n"
"\n"
"Where there are no intervening anchors, you can anchor to the Nth paragraph of e.g. poetry or a keyterm definition, by specifying the paragraph number after an = sign. For example, GLO k.Harp=2 or PSA 23.4=3. This can avoid the need to insert an explicit milestone to anchor a cutout if there is a page or column break after the start of the verse."
msgstr "锚点用于指定图片出现在书卷的哪一页。图片与其在文本中的锚点出现在同一页。可以将锚点参考调整几节，以改变图片出现的页面。\n"
"\n"
"锚点参考必须由卷代码组成，（双语对照时）后面可跟 L 或 R，然后是一个空格，再是包含点（句号）的卷内位置。在圣经经卷中，卷内位置为章.节，其中的节须与 \\v 的值完全一致。在其他书卷中，卷内位置可以是任何内容，只要在该卷中唯一并且包含一个点（句号）即可。\n"
"\n"
"双语对照的锚点参考在 3 个字母的卷代码后加 L 或 R 后缀，表示图片与主要文本（L）还是次要文本（R）相关联。\n"
"\n"
"在词汇表卷（GLO）中，对 \\k Keywords\\k* 有特别支持：卷内位置 k.关键词 会将图片锚定到相应的词条。卷内位置必须与 \\k 关键词或短语\\k* 的值去掉空格后一致。例如，\n"
"\n"
"    GLO k.Altar - 将链接到 \\k Altar\\k*\n"
"    GLO k.JohntheBaptist - 将把图片链接到\n"
"               词汇表条目 \\k John the Baptist\\k*\n"
"\n"
"输入 GLO k. 之后，可以复制并粘贴词汇表中的单词或短语，PTXprint 会自动去除空格。\n"
"\n"
"如果中间没有其他锚点，可以通过在 = 号后指定段落编号，锚定到诗歌或关键词条定义等内容的第 N 段。例如 GLO k.Harp=2 或 PSA 23.4=3。如果在节开始之后出现分页或分栏，这样可以避免插入明确的里程碑标记来锚定嵌入图。"

#: temp.glade:28571
msgid "Caption\n"
"Ref:"
msgstr "说明\n"
"引用："

#: temp.glade:28587
msgid "The reference in the caption can be a single Ch:Vs or \n"
"a range of verses 6:17-29. This Caption Ref is different\n"
"from and independent of the Anchor Ref setting.\n"
msgstr "说明中的引用可以是单个章:节，也可以是\n"
"一段经文范围，如 6:17-29。此说明引用\n"
"与锚点参考的设置不同，且相互独立。\n"

#: temp.glade:28605
msgid "Description:\n"
"(Alt Text)"
msgstr "描述：\n"
"(替代文本)"

#: temp.glade:28633
msgid "Note that any changes you make to the filename\n"
"here will NOT automatically be updated in the\n"
"Paratext USFM files. Please edit/fit the figure\n"
"information manually in Paratext if you change\n"
"things here in PTXprint."
msgstr "请注意，在此处对文件名所做的任何更改\n"
"都不会自动更新到\n"
"Paratext 的 USFM 文件中。如果在\n"
"PTXprint 中修改了这里的内容，请在 Paratext 中\n"
"手动编辑相应的插图信息。"

#: temp.glade:28667
msgid "For commonly used series of illustrations, PTXprint\n"
"can automatically generate the appropriate copyright\n"
"attribution statement(s) as part of the colophon text.\n"
"\n"
"For other less-known artists' you may enter the appropriate\n"
"copyright information which is usually in the format of:\n"
"   by Artist Name © Year, Entity Name and License Type."
msgstr "对于常用的系列插图，PTXprint\n"
"可以自动生成相应的版权\n"
"归属声明，作为版权页文字的一部分。\n"
"\n"
"对于其他不太知名的艺术家，可以按以下格式\n"
"输入相应的版权信息：\n"
"   作者：艺术家姓名 © 年份，机构名称及许可证类型。"

#: temp.glade:28675
msgid "Copyright\n"
"Attribution:"
msgstr "版权\n"
"归属："

#: temp.glade:28689
msgid "There are several shortcuts you can use:\n"
"   (c) --> ©  the copyright sign\n"
"   (r) --> ®  to denote registered trademarks\n"
"   (tm) --> ™  to denote trademarks in general"
msgstr "可以使用以下几个快捷方式：\n"
"   (c) --> ©  版权符号\n"
"   (r) --> ®  表示注册商标\n"
"   (tm) --> ™  表示一般商标"

#: temp.glade:28694
msgid "by Artist Name © Year, Entity Name and License Type"
msgstr "作者：艺术家姓名 © 年份，机构名称及许可证类型"

#: temp.glade:28707
msgid "The frame size determines how large the picture\n"
"will appear on the page.\n"
"\n"
"Span Width only allows a Top or Bottom vertical placement.\n"
"Column Width allows several other more precise placement \n"
"options: Before Verse, After Paragraph, or Cutout; and these\n"
"can have Left/Inner or Right/Outer Horizontal positioning set. \n"
" \n"
"When using single column layout, there is no\n"
"difference between Column Width and Span Width."
msgstr "图框大小决定图片\n"
"在页面上显示的大小。\n"
"\n"
"跨宽仅允许在顶部或底部垂直放置。\n"
"栏宽允许其他几种更精确的放置\n"
"选项：节前、段落后或镂空；这些选项\n"
"还可以设置左/内或右/外水平位置。\n"
" \n"
"使用单栏布局时，栏宽和跨宽没有\n"
"区别。"

#: temp.glade:28730 temp.glade:28782
msgid "Several options here are extensions to the normal USFM\n"
"markup standard for illustrations and are not expected\n"
"to work in other software. But PTXprint allows a greater\n"
"level of control in placing pictures.\n"
"\n"
"Top: Above everything except the header line\n"
"Bottom: Below all verse text (and footnotes in diglot)\n"
"Before Verse: 'Here' where defined or before its Anchor Ref\n"
"After Paragraph: After this paragraph\n"
"Cutout: A notch/corner cut out of the text, starting at current line\n"
"\n"
"The above options may have other positioning parameters such\n"
"as: Left, Right, Center, no. of lines (up or down)."
msgstr "这里的几个选项是对USFM插图标记标准的扩展，\n"
"其他软件可能无法识别。但PTXprint在放置图片时\n"
"提供了更多控制。\n"
"\n"
"顶部：位于除页眉行以外的所有内容上方\n"
"底部：位于所有经文文本下方（双语对照中还在脚注下方）\n"
"节前：在已定义的“此处”，或在其锚点参考之前\n"
"段落后：位于此段落之后\n"
"镂空：从当前行开始，在文本中切出一个缺口/转角\n"
"\n"
"以上选项可能还有其他定位参数，\n"
"例如：左、右、居中、行数（向上或向下）。"

#: temp.glade:28758
msgid "An image (illustration) can be scaled to the\n"
"given size. This is particularly useful for\n"
"cutout images, and can prevent them from\n"
"taking up too much space within the text."
msgstr "可以将图片（插图）缩放到\n"
"指定大小。这对镂空\n"
"图片特别有用，可以避免其\n"
"在文本中占用过多空间。"

#: temp.glade:28824
msgid "The frame size determines the boundaries of where the\n"
"picture will appear on the page.\n"
"\n"
"Span Width only allows a Top or Bottom vertical placement.\n"
"\n"
"Column Width allows several other more precise placement \n"
"options: Before Verse, After Paragraph, or Cutout; and these\n"
"can have Left/Inner or Right/Outer Horizontal positioning set. \n"
" \n"
"Page (in Margins) is intended for pictures that will cover an\n"
"entire page (i.e. preventing any scripture text from being on\n"
"that page), but will still show the header.\n"
"\n"
"Page (to Edge) is intended for pictures (or more commonly\n"
"for maps) to fill the entire page, with no margins at all. \n"
"Captions should not be used with 'Page (to Edge)' images."
msgstr "图框大小决定图片在页面上出现位置的边界。\n"
"\n"
"跨宽仅允许在顶部或底部垂直放置。\n"
"\n"
"栏宽允许其他几种更精确的放置\n"
"选项：节前、段落后或镂空；这些选项\n"
"还可以设置左/内或右/外水平位置。\n"
" \n"
"页面（页边距以内）用于覆盖整个页面的图片（即该页面\n"
"不会出现任何经文），\n"
"但仍会显示页眉。\n"
"\n"
"页面（到页面边缘）用于填满整个页面的图片（更常用于地图），完全没有页边距。\n"
"图片说明不应与“页面（到页面边缘）”的图片一起使用。"

#: temp.glade:28917
msgid "It is good typesetting practice to make people\n"
"look outwards from the gutter, so you can set\n"
"whether the image is to be mirrored just on \n"
"odd pages or even pages.\n"
"\n"
"Some artists' pictures do not take into account\n"
"the \"dirty left-hand\" culture. For example, it would\n"
"be \"awkward\" to use a picture where Jesus is healing\n"
"a person using his LEFT hand! What an insult!\n"
"\n"
"So this option allows the image to be mirrored (on\n"
"both pages) in order to make the left become right.\n"
"But you should check carefully to see what other\n"
"unwanted side effects this mirroring may cause.\n"
"\n"
"Note: This option will be grayed out if the picture has  \n"
"the \"Never Mirror\" setting checked on the Checklist tab."
msgstr "排版时的良好做法是让图中人物\n"
"朝向装订线边距的外侧，因此可以设置\n"
"图片是仅在奇数页还是偶数页上\n"
"进行镜像。\n"
"\n"
"一些艺术家的图片没有考虑到\n"
"“左手不洁”的文化。例如，\n"
"图片中耶稣用左手\n"
"为人治病，在这些文化中会显得别扭，甚至冒犯！\n"
"\n"
"因此，此选项允许对图片进行镜像（在\n"
"两种页面上），使左边变为右边。\n"
"但应仔细检查，看镜像处理是否造成了其他\n"
"不想要的副作用。\n"
"\n"
"注意：如果在“检查表”选项卡上\n"
"勾选了该图片的“永不镜像”设置，此选项将呈灰色。"

#: temp.glade:28935
msgid "Mirror:"
msgstr "镜像："

#: temp.glade:28950
msgid "Never = The image will never be mirrored\n"
"Odd = Mirrored only if image ends up on an odd page\n"
"Even = Mirrored only if image ends up on an even page\n"
"Always = Always mirrored (regardless of where it ends up)\n"
"\n"
"Note that if this option is grayed out, it is because \n"
"you have already restricted the mirroring options \n"
"on the Checklist tab."
msgstr "永不 = 图片永不镜像\n"
"奇数页 = 仅当图片位于奇数页时镜像\n"
"偶数页 = 仅当图片位于偶数页时镜像\n"
"总是 = 始终镜像（无论图片位于哪一页）\n"
"\n"
"注意，如果此选项呈灰色，是因为\n"
"已在“检查表”选项卡上限制了镜像选项。"

#: temp.glade:28985 temp.glade:29012
msgid "Some vertical position options allow a picture\n"
"to be moved up or down by a number of lines\n"
"or paragraphs.\n"
"\n"
"-Negative (minus) values specify to move UP.\n"
"+Positive (plus) values specify to move DOWN.\n"
"\n"
"Negative counts for cutouts raise the image,\n"
"but the cutout will not affect earlier paragraphs. \n"
"Note that negative and fractional paragraph \n"
"counts are invalid."
msgstr "某些垂直位置选项允许将图片\n"
"向上或向下移动若干行\n"
"或若干段落。\n"
"\n"
"-负值（减号）表示向上移动。\n"
"+正值（加号）表示向下移动。\n"
"\n"
"镂空图片使用负值会使图片上移，\n"
"但镂空不会影响前面的段落。\n"
"注意，段落数不能为负数或小数。"

#: temp.glade:29064
msgid "Can be used in Print/PDF publications. "
msgstr "可以在打印/PDF出版物中使用。 "

#: temp.glade:29080
msgid "Can be used in mobile phone Apps. "
msgstr "可以用于手机应用程序。 "

#: temp.glade:29096
msgid "Can be used on websites. "
msgstr "可以在网页上使用。 "

#: temp.glade:29117
msgid "If the image is from the recognized\n"
"set of pictures commonly used in\n"
"Scripture publications, then there is\n"
"no need to fill in the Copyright \n"
"Attribution field, as this will be\n"
"generated automatically for you."
msgstr "如果图片来自圣经出版物中\n"
"常用的已知图片集，\n"
"则无需填写版权归属字段，\n"
"因为该字段会自动生成。"

#: temp.glade:29125
msgid "Automatic"
msgstr "自动的"

#: temp.glade:29137
msgid "© ..."
msgstr "© ..."

#: temp.glade:29142
msgid "Credit Overlays...\n"
"Some artists (e.g. David C Cook) require that\n"
"each image has a copyright message printed\n"
"on the image itself. The text and location can\n"
"be set here."
msgstr "版权叠加...\n"
"有些艺术家（例如David C Cook）要求\n"
"每张图片都要在\n"
"图像上打印版权信息。\n"
"可以在这里设置这些信息的文字和位置。"

#: temp.glade:29164
msgid "Credit overlay position and style"
msgstr "版权叠加的位置和样式"

#: temp.glade:29210
msgid "Click to edit the Figure Caption properties on the Styles tab."
msgstr "单击以编辑“样式”选项卡上的图片说明属性。"

#: temp.glade:29246
msgid "Extra:"
msgstr "附加的："

#: temp.glade:29355
msgid "Use this tab to change the position, location, size \n"
"or orientation of the images.\n"
"\n"
"Note: Any changes you make here will NOT be \n"
"reflected in the Paratext USFM files. So if you are \n"
"changing an illustration, its caption or frame size\n"
"(column or span), then it is advisable to do so\n"
"in Paratext before regenerating the PicList here."
msgstr "使用此选项卡更改图片的位置、地点、大小\n"
"或方向。\n"
"\n"
"注意：在此所做的任何更改都不会\n"
"反映到Paratext的USFM文件中。因此，如果需要\n"
"修改插图、其说明或图框大小\n"
"（栏或跨），建议先在Paratext中修改，\n"
"然后再在此处重新生成图片列表。"

#: temp.glade:29363
msgid "Details"
msgstr "详细信息"

#: temp.glade:29420
msgid "Is there anything confusing or misleading in this image that the reader might misunderstand if they look at this picture apart from the text? Yes and no are both appropriate answers as some images may need to be seen alongside text in order to be understood."
msgstr "如果脱离文字单独看这张图片，图中是否有令读者困惑、\n"
"容易误解的内容？回答“是”或“否”都可以，因为有些图片\n"
"需要结合文字才能理解。"

#: temp.glade:29422
msgid "Is it clear what is happening in this image?"
msgstr "是否清楚这张图片里发生的事？"

#: temp.glade:29433
msgid "First consider whether this picture is appropriate and culturally acceptable in any publications for this project."
msgstr "首先要考虑的是在这个项目的所有出版物里，这张图片是否合宜，文化上是否可接受。"

#: temp.glade:29435
msgid "Across Various Publications:"
msgstr "在各种出版物中："

#: temp.glade:29449 temp.glade:29717 temp.glade:29771
msgid "Yes"
msgstr "是"

#: temp.glade:29467 temp.glade:29735 temp.glade:29789
msgid "No"
msgstr "否"

#: temp.glade:29505
msgid "Be sure that there is nothing offensive or inappropriate in this image. This could be the way people are clothed, what actions they are doing, how they are depicted, etc. “Culturally Appropriate” means this image is in a style from this culture or a related one, “Acceptable” means this picture might be from a different culture or in a different style, but there are no issues using it. “Inappropriate” means there are issues that should prevent this image from being used. Answering “Inappropriate” will help avoid this image being used in other publications."
msgstr "请确保这张图片中没有任何冒犯或不恰当的内容，例如人物的穿着、正在做的事情、被描绘的方式等。“文化适当”指这张图片的风格来自本文化或相关文化；“可接受”指这张图片可能来自不同文化或采用不同风格，但使用上没有问题；“不恰当”指存在问题，不应使用这张图片。选择“不恰当”有助于避免这张图片被用于其他出版物。"

#: temp.glade:29507
msgid "Is this image acceptable in your culture?"
msgstr "这张图片在本文化中是否可接受？"

#: temp.glade:29518
msgid "Sometimes mirroring (reversing) an image makes it\n"
"acceptable since a left hand becomes a right hand, etc.\n"
"\n"
"Some artists' pictures do not take into account\n"
"the \"dirty left-hand\" culture. For example, it would\n"
"be \"awkward\" to use a picture where Jesus is healing\n"
"a person using his left hand!"
msgstr "有时将图片镜像（反转）后就可以接受，因为左手会变成右手，等等。\n"
"\n"
"一些艺术家的作品没有考虑到“左手不洁”的文化。例如，使用耶稣用左手医治病人的图片会显得“别扭”！"

#: temp.glade:29526
msgid "Would the image be culturally acceptable if \n"
"the image was mirrored (left becomes right)?"
msgstr "如果将图片镜像（左变右），\n"
"在文化上是否可接受？"

#: temp.glade:29538 temp.glade:29860
msgid "Now consider whether there are any issues with using this picture in this particular publication (config-specific)."
msgstr "现在考虑在这个特定出版物中使用这张图片是否有任何问题（针对具体配置）。"

#: temp.glade:29540
msgid "In This Publication:"
msgstr "本出版物："

#: temp.glade:29556
msgid "Consider how this image is used alongside the text and what function it serves. Maybe it depicts a building or item from a biblical culture, or a scene from a story."
msgstr "考虑这张图片如何与文字配合使用，以及它起到什么作用。例如，它可能描绘了圣经文化中的建筑或物品，或故事中的某个场景。"

#: temp.glade:29558
msgid "Is this picture intended for: clarification,\n"
"story enhancement, filler, unknown?"
msgstr "这张图片的用途是：说明、\n"
"增强故事、填充版面，还是不明？"

#: temp.glade:29570
msgid "Does the image support what the text is saying? As they read the passage does the image help in their understanding?"
msgstr "图片是否支持文字所表达的内容？读者阅读这段经文时，图片是否有助于理解？"

#: temp.glade:29572
msgid "In the context of this passage, is it clear \n"
"what is happening in this image?"
msgstr "结合这段经文的上下文，\n"
"是否能清楚看出这张图片中发生了什么？"

#: temp.glade:29584
msgid "For example, do the colors have the same meaning in the local culture? Is there anything in the background that is distracting from the story? Are there any objects, gestures, or other things that imply something unintended or that isn’t in the passage? Are there any anachronisms in the picture (a minaret in Bethlehem)?"
msgstr "例如，颜色在当地文化中是否含义相同？背景中是否有分散对故事注意力的内容？是否有任何物体、手势或其他内容暗示了非本意或经文中没有的意思？图片中是否有时代错误（例如伯利恒出现宣礼塔）？"

#: temp.glade:29586
msgid "Does the image communicate something \n"
"that it should not in this particular context?"
msgstr "在这个特定情境下，图片是否传达了\n"
"不应传达的信息？"

#: temp.glade:29598
msgid "Do the images and their style fit with the type of publication, i.e. Scripture, children’s materials, lectionary, etc.? Are people and actions depicted in acceptable ways?"
msgstr "图片及其风格是否适合出版物的类型，例如经文、儿童读物、读经本等？人物和行为的描绘方式是否可接受？"

#: temp.glade:29600
msgid "Is the image appropriate for the publication?"
msgstr "这张图片是否适合用于本出版物？"

#: temp.glade:29613
msgid "Select the level to which this illustration\n"
"is acceptable in the receptor culture."
msgstr "选择这幅插图在接收文化中\n"
"的可接受程度。"

#: temp.glade:29630
msgid "OK to\n"
"mirror"
msgstr "可以\n"
"镜像"

#: temp.glade:29636
msgid "It is fine to mirror the image if needed. It would\n"
"not change the impact or response of the readers."
msgstr "如有需要，可以将图片镜像。\n"
"这不会改变对读者的影响或读者的反应。"

#: temp.glade:29651
msgid "Never\n"
"mirror"
msgstr "永不\n"
"做镜像处理"

#: temp.glade:29657
msgid "Ensure that this image is always shown\n"
"as currently depicted in the preview. Do\n"
"NOT allow it to be mirrored (reversed)."
msgstr "确保始终按预览中当前的样子显示此图片。\n"
"不允许镜像（反转）。"

#: temp.glade:29673
msgid "Always\n"
"mirror"
msgstr "始终做\n"
"镜像处理"

#: temp.glade:29679
msgid "Ensure that this image is always mirrored from\n"
"what is currently shown in the preview. Therefore\n"
"actions being done with the left hand will show as\n"
"being done with the right hand, and vice versa."
msgstr "确保此图片始终相对于\n"
"预览中当前显示的样子做镜像处理。因此，\n"
"用左手做的动作将显示为用右手做的，\n"
"反之亦然。"

#: temp.glade:29700
msgid "Select the reason for including the\n"
"illustration in this particular publication."
msgstr "选择在这个特定出版物中\n"
"使用该插图的原因。"

#: temp.glade:29753 temp.glade:29839
msgid "Unchecked"
msgstr "未检查"

#: temp.glade:29811
msgid "Select the appropriateness of the\n"
"illustration within this publication."
msgstr "选择该插图在本出版物中\n"
"的适当程度。"

#: temp.glade:29862
msgid "Consultant Approval:"
msgstr "顾问批准："

#: temp.glade:29879
msgid "The most recent date that the\n"
"consultant approval updated."
msgstr "咨询师审核更新的最近日期。"

#: temp.glade:29885
msgid "Date"
msgstr "日期"

#: temp.glade:29902
msgid "Initials"
msgstr "首字母"

#: temp.glade:29916
msgid "any publication"
msgstr "任何出版物"

#: temp.glade:29933
msgid "this publication"
msgstr "此出版物"

#: temp.glade:29950
msgid "Approved to\n"
"be used in:"
msgstr "批准\n"
"用于："

#: temp.glade:29969
msgid "     "
msgstr ""

#: temp.glade:29982
msgid "By:"
msgstr "由："

#: temp.glade:30051
msgid "Notes About This Picture:"
msgstr "关于此图片的注释："

#: temp.glade:30131
msgid "Pictures are best used in situations where:\n"
"1. The physical situation is not understood, or not common in the target culture.\n"
"2. Where the physical situation is important to understanding the meaning of the passage (e.g., the type of clothing is often not important, but in some passages it might be).\n"
"3. Where they help the reader to understand the passage.\n"
"4. Where it entices the reader to read the passage."
msgstr "图片最好用在以下情况：\n"
"1. 实际情况不易被理解，或在目标文化中不常见。\n"
"2. 实际情况对理解经文段落的含义很重要（例如，衣着类型通常不重要，但在某些段落中可能很重要）。\n"
"3. 有助于读者理解经文段落。\n"
"4. 能吸引读者阅读该段落。"

#: temp.glade:30136
msgid "Questions to Consider"
msgstr "要考虑的问题"

#: temp.glade:30165
msgid "This tab encourages you to think through\n"
"the appropriateness of the pictures used\n"
"in this publication, as well as other contexts."
msgstr "此选项卡帮助思考本出版物中所用图片\n"
"是否恰当，以及在其他场合使用时\n"
"是否适宜。"

#: temp.glade:30168
msgid "Checklist"
msgstr "检查表"

#: temp.glade:30263
msgid "Manipulate the pictures to be used\n"
"in the publication. Control everything\n"
"from quality to position, from captions\n"
"to copyrights."
msgstr "管理出版物中要使用的图片，\n"
"控制从质量到位置、\n"
"从图片说明到版权的各项设置。"

#: temp.glade:30312
msgid "Use Default Header Settings for Diglot"
msgstr "使用双语对照的默认页眉设置"

#: temp.glade:30317
msgid "Checking this option will override\n"
"the header settings and place the\n"
"Reference Ranges on the outer edges\n"
"and Page Number in (or near) the middle."
msgstr "勾选此选项将覆盖页眉设置，\n"
"把参考范围放在外侧边缘，\n"
"并把页码放在中间（或附近）。"

#: temp.glade:30333
msgid "Adjust Center Header Based on Column Widths"
msgstr "根据栏宽调整居中页眉"

#: temp.glade:30338
msgid "If the column widths of the two sides of the\n"
"diglot are unequal, PTXprint can ensure that\n"
"the content of the center header matches the\n"
"position of the gutter (space between the two\n"
"different columns)."
msgstr "如果双语对照两侧的\n"
"栏宽不等，PTXprint可以确保\n"
"居中页眉的内容与装订线边距的\n"
"位置相匹配（两个\n"
"不同栏之间的空间）。"

#: temp.glade:30376
msgid "Vertical Rule in Notes Area"
msgstr "注释区内的垂直线"

#: temp.glade:30381
msgid "Add a vertical rule between the two\n"
"sides of the notes area of the diglot."
msgstr "在双语对照的注释区两侧\n"
"之间添加垂直线。"

#: temp.glade:30396
msgid "Join with Rule Above"
msgstr "与上面的线连起来"

#: temp.glade:30401
msgid "To prevent a small gap in the line\n"
"allow the vertical line to extend\n"
"down into the notes area."
msgstr "为了防止行中出现小的间隙，\n"
"允许垂直线\n"
"延伸到注释区。"

#: temp.glade:30420
msgid "Separate Notes in Two Columns"
msgstr "把注释分成两栏"

#: temp.glade:30425
msgid "If this option is disabled, the footnotes from\n"
"both sides of the diglot get merged together\n"
"and are interspersed one after the other.\n"
"\n"
"Depending on the scripts and text direction,\n"
"this may or may not be desirable. If in doubt,\n"
"leave this option checked ON."
msgstr "如果禁用此选项，双语对照\n"
"两侧的脚注将合并在一起，\n"
"并依次交错排列。\n"
"\n"
"视文字和文本方向而定，\n"
"这样做可能合适，也可能不合适。如有疑问，\n"
"请勾选此选项。"

#: temp.glade:30480
msgid "Left-click to change values as needed.\n"
"Right-click to show the context menu."
msgstr "左键单击可按需更改数值。\n"
"右键单击可显示上下文菜单。"

#: temp.glade:30543
msgid "LR,A/B"
msgstr "LR,A/B"

#: temp.glade:30578
msgid "Merging mode:"
msgstr "合并模式："

#: temp.glade:30697
msgid "Layout:"
msgstr "布局："

#: temp.glade:30709 temp.glade:30732
msgid "Some books (e.g. Introduction, Glossary, Back Matter, etc.)\n"
"in a diglot publication should not be merged to appear\n"
"side-by-side, but instead need to occur one after the other.\n"
"\n"
"Add the 3-letter book codes for any books that should \n"
"not be merged. These will appear one after the other."
msgstr "双语对照出版物中，有些卷（如导言、词汇表、后记等）\n"
"不应合并为并排显示，而应一卷接一卷地依次出现。\n"
"\n"
"添加不应合并的各卷的 3 个字母卷代码。\n"
"这些卷将依次出现。"

#: temp.glade:30717
msgid "Use Serial Layout\n"
"for These Books:"
msgstr "对这些卷使用\n"
"顺序排版："

#: temp.glade:30741
msgid "FRT BAK GLO XXA XXB"
msgstr "FRT BAK GLO XXA XXB"

#: temp.glade:30743
msgid "e.g. FRT BAK GLO XXA XXB"
msgstr "例如：FRT BAK GLO XXA XXB"

#: temp.glade:30754
msgid "Diglot (or Polyglot)"
msgstr "双语对照（或多语对照）"

#: temp.glade:30787
msgid "Create a diglot publication by selecting \n"
"a secondary project and configuration."
msgstr "选择次要项目和配置，\n"
"创建双语对照出版物。"

#: lib/ptxprint/gtkstyleditor.py:65 lib/ptxprint/gtkview.py:3007 temp.glade:30790
msgid "Diglot"
msgstr "双语对照"

#: temp.glade:30832 temp.glade:30968
msgid "The length of the Thumb Tab measured in millimeters (mm)."
msgstr "拇指索引标签的长度，单位为毫米（mm）。"

#: temp.glade:30834
msgid "Length:"
msgstr "长度："

#: temp.glade:30846 temp.glade:30861
msgid "The height of the Thumb Tab measured in millimeters (mm)."
msgstr "拇指索引标签的高度，单位为毫米（mm）。"

#: temp.glade:30848
msgid "Height:"
msgstr "高度："

#: temp.glade:30881
msgid "Thumb Tabs usually use a dark color\n"
"for the background with a light color\n"
"(or white) for the foreground text.\n"
"\n"
"The background color is set here, but\n"
"the foreground text color needs to be\n"
"set by clicking the Edit Style link."
msgstr "拇指索引标签通常使用深色\n"
"作背景，浅色（或白色）\n"
"作前景文字颜色。\n"
"\n"
"此处设置背景颜色，\n"
"前景文字颜色需单击“编辑样式”链接来设置。"

#: temp.glade:30889
msgid "Tab Color:"
msgstr "标签颜色："

#: temp.glade:30905
msgid "Thumb Tab Background Color"
msgstr "拇指索引标签背景颜色"

#: temp.glade:30916
msgid "Rotate Tabs:"
msgstr "旋转标签："

#: temp.glade:30921
msgid "Rotates the tabs so that the text runs along the edge of the page. This works well for narrow margins, but may result in fewer tab positions per page."
msgstr "旋转标签，使文字沿页面边缘排列。页边距较窄时效果很好，但每页可用的标签位置可能会减少。"

#: temp.glade:30939
msgid "Number of\n"
"Tab Positions:"
msgstr "标签位置数量："

#: temp.glade:30992 temp.glade:31094
msgid "<span background=\"black\" foreground=\"white\" font-weight=\"bold\">  Vertical  </span>"
msgstr "<span background=\"black\" foreground=\"white\" font-weight=\"bold\">  垂直  </span>"

#: temp.glade:31009 temp.glade:31125
msgid "<span background=\"black\" foreground=\"white\" font-weight=\"bold\">  Horizontal  </span>"
msgstr "<span background=\"black\" foreground=\"white\" font-weight=\"bold\">  水平  </span>"

#: temp.glade:31023
msgid "When several shorter adjacent books occur, it is\n"
"common to group them together to use the same\n"
"tab position (but still have differently named tabs)."
msgstr "当出现几卷相邻的较短书卷时，\n"
"通常将它们归为一组，使用同一个\n"
"标签位置（但标签名称仍各不相同）。"

#: temp.glade:31028
msgid "Grouped Tabs:"
msgstr "分组标签："

#: temp.glade:31041
msgid "List book IDs of short books to be grouped together\n"
"at the same tab position. Use spaces between book \n"
"IDs, and use ; to separate groups. There is no need to\n"
"list all the book IDs here - only the special ones which\n"
"need to share the same tab position.\n"
"\n"
"For example: PHM TIT; 1JN 2JN 3JN JUD"
msgstr "列出需要归为一组、共用同一标签位置的\n"
"短卷的卷代码。卷代码之间用空格分隔，\n"
"各组之间用；分隔。无需在此列出\n"
"所有卷代码，只需列出\n"
"需要共用同一标签位置的特殊卷。\n"
"\n"
"例如：PHM TIT; 1JN 2JN 3JN JUD"

#: temp.glade:31063
msgid "If you choose to Rotate the tabs, there are various options as to how these should be oriented. The preview (right) will show how these will appear on facing pages."
msgstr "选择旋转标签后，可通过多种选项设置标签的朝向。右侧预览将显示这些标签在对页上的显示效果。"

#: temp.glade:31151
msgid "Restart Tabs at MAT"
msgstr "在 MAT 处重新开始标签"

#: temp.glade:31156
msgid "Normally books will follow sequentially and if the next tab would be off the bottom of the page, then it will be set to the top for a new cycle of tabs. Setting this starts a new cycle at the start of the New Testament (Matthew)."
msgstr "通常书卷按顺序排列，如果下一个标签会超出页面底部，则将其放到顶部，开始新一轮标签。选中此项后，将从新约开头（马太福音）开始新一轮标签。"

#: temp.glade:31173
msgid "ColorVal"
msgstr "色彩值"

#: temp.glade:31254
msgid "Tab Text:"
msgstr "标签文本："

#: temp.glade:31264
msgid "\\toc3"
msgstr "\\toc3"

#: temp.glade:31290
msgid "\\zthumbtab"
msgstr "\\Zthumbtab"

#: lib/ptxprint/pdf_viewer.py:59 temp.glade:31325
msgid "Edit Style"
msgstr "编辑样式"

#: temp.glade:31330
msgid "Click to jump to the appropriate\n"
"(\\toc3 or \\zthumbtab) marker in\n"
"the style editor to change the\n"
"formatting of the thumb tabs."
msgstr "单击可跳转到样式编辑器中相应的（\\toc3 或 \\zthumbtab）标记，以更改拇指索引标签的格式。"

#: temp.glade:31354
msgid "Only Show on Odd Pages"
msgstr "只显示在奇数页上"

#: temp.glade:31359
msgid "When printing thumb tabs on thin paper,\n"
"it is preferable to only print these tabs on\n"
"a single side of the page (the odd pages)."
msgstr "在薄纸上打印拇指索引标签时，最好只在页面的单面（奇数页）上打印这些标签。"

#: temp.glade:31377
msgid "Thumb Tabs"
msgstr "拇指索引标签"

#: temp.glade:31484 temp.glade:32137
msgid "Shift:"
msgstr "移位："

#: temp.glade:31544 temp.glade:31753
msgid "PDF border (Legacy)"
msgstr "PDF边框（旧版）"

#: temp.glade:31566 temp.glade:31776
msgid "Dynamic Border"
msgstr "动态边框"

#: temp.glade:31594
msgid "If Section Headings sometimes extend to more \n"
"than one line, then a static PDF section heading\n"
"is unlikely to work. Instead, a dynamically\n"
"generated decorative section heading needs to\n"
"be set up to grow/shrink with the content of\n"
"the heading. Use this link to show the special\n"
"style, which needs to be enabled and defined."
msgstr "如果章节标题有时会超过一行，\n"
"静态的 PDF 章节标题很可能不适用。\n"
"此时需要设置动态生成的装饰性章节标题，\n"
"使其随标题内容自动扩大/缩小。\n"
"单击此链接可显示该特殊样式，\n"
"该样式需要先启用并定义。"

#: temp.glade:31632
msgid "Section Headings"
msgstr "分段标题"

#: temp.glade:31637
msgid "Section Headings may be adorned with\n"
"a special graphic. Ensure that there is\n"
"adequate space - both horizontal as well\n"
"as vertical to make sure all headings fit."
msgstr "分段标题可以用特殊图形装饰。请确保水平和垂直方向都有足够的空间，使所有标题都能容纳。"

#: temp.glade:31695
msgid "Full page"
msgstr "整页"

#: temp.glade:31700
msgid "If set, the border is expanded to the full page. Otherwise it is expanded only to the gutter margins."
msgstr "如果选中，边框将扩展到整个页面。否则只扩展到装订线边距。"

#: temp.glade:31737
msgid "Click to edit the properties of the\n"
"Text Border (which is controlled by\n"
"the \\textborder style on the Styles tab)."
msgstr "单击可编辑\n"
"文本边框的属性（可通过\n"
"样式选项卡上的 \\textborder 样式进行控制）。"

#: temp.glade:31548 temp.glade:31757
msgid "Use an existing PDF Border for the\n"
"entire publication."
msgstr "为整本出版物使用现有的PDF边框。"

#: temp.glade:31570 temp.glade:31780
msgid "Place a decorative border only around \n"
"the Scripture text (excludes introductions, \n"
"footnotes and other peripheral material)."
msgstr "仅在 \n"
"经文（不包括引言、 \n"
"脚注和其他外围材料）周围加上装饰性边框。"

#: temp.glade:31799
msgid "Page Border"
msgstr "页面边框"

#: temp.glade:31804
msgid "Place a uniform-sized decorative border\n"
"on every page regardless of content."
msgstr "在每一页上放置大小统一的装饰性边框，\n"
"无论页面内容如何。"

#: temp.glade:31828
msgid "Click to edit the properties of the\n"
"Page Border (which is controlled by\n"
"the \\pageborder style on the Styles tab)."
msgstr "单击可编辑\n"
"页面边框的属性（该属性由\n"
"样式选项卡上的\\pageborder 样式控制）。"

#: temp.glade:31875
msgid "There are different kinds of borders that\n"
"can be applied to the publication. \n"
"\n"
"Note that if you use a border, it is likely\n"
"that you will need to adjust the margins\n"
"to make it fit."
msgstr "可以对出版物应用不同种类的边框。\n"
"\n"
"请注意，使用边框后，很可能需要调整页边距，以使其适合。"

#: temp.glade:31986
msgid "End of Book Decoration"
msgstr "书末装饰"

#: temp.glade:31991
msgid "The end of each book may be adorned \n"
"with a special graphic."
msgstr "每卷的结尾可以用特殊图形装饰。"

#: temp.glade:32030
msgid "End of Ayah"
msgstr "节结束符（Ayah）"

#: temp.glade:32035
msgid "Use the End of Ayah character in the\n"
"font to decorate the verse number."
msgstr "使用字体中的节结束符（Ayah）字符来装饰节号。"

#: temp.glade:32052
msgid "Verse Border Graphic"
msgstr "节边框图形"

#: temp.glade:32057
msgid "Use a PDF graphic to decorate the verse \n"
"number. You may need to also adjust the\n"
"font properties to ensure the verse numbers\n"
"fit within the graphic."
msgstr "使用 PDF 图形来装饰节\n"
"号。可能还需调整\n"
"字体属性，以确保节号\n"
"能放入图形内。"

#: temp.glade:32133 temp.glade:32151
msgid "Vertical shift in pts of the verse decorator image.\n"
"  + values shift the decorator upwards\n"
"  - values shift the decorator downwards"
msgstr "节号装饰图像的垂直偏移量（单位：磅）。\n"
"  正值使装饰图像上移\n"
"  负值使装饰图像下移"

#: temp.glade:32199
msgid "Move Ayah"
msgstr "移动 Ayah"

#: temp.glade:32204
msgid "This option moves the Ayah\n"
"to the end of the verse. "
msgstr "此选项将 Ayah\n"
"移到节末。 "

#: temp.glade:32082 temp.glade:32225
msgid "Click to edit the \\v marker's properties on the Styles tab."
msgstr "单击可在“样式”选项卡上编辑 \\v 标记的属性。"

#: temp.glade:32255
msgid "Verse Number Decorator"
msgstr "节号装饰"

#: temp.glade:32260
msgid "Verse numbers can be decorated using\n"
"either of the options shown below."
msgstr "可使用下面显示的任一选项\n"
"来装饰节号。"

#: temp.glade:32312
msgid "Adjust the styling of the dynamic \n"
"borders around book titles."
msgstr "调整卷标题周围\n"
"动态边框的样式。"

#: temp.glade:32347
msgid "Book Title Borders"
msgstr "卷标题边框"

#: temp.glade:32352
msgid "Dynamic borders can be applied to\n"
"book titles (\\mt1 and \\mt2). Styling\n"
"can be adjusted using the link below."
msgstr "可为卷标题（\\mt1 和 \\mt2）\n"
"添加动态边框。可使用下方链接\n"
"调整样式。"

#: temp.glade:32373
msgid "Ornamental Decorations"
msgstr "装饰性修饰"

#: temp.glade:32378
msgid "Enable this option to make use of\n"
"ornamental borders, rules & verses.\n"
"\n"
"Some cultures place a high value on\n"
"such decorative features in scripture\n"
"publications."
msgstr "启用此选项可使用\n"
"装饰性边框、分隔线和节。\n"
"\n"
"有些文化非常重视\n"
"经文出版物中的\n"
"此类装饰性特征。"

#: temp.glade:32412
msgid "Tabs+Borders"
msgstr "索引标+边框"

#: temp.glade:32449 temp.glade:32466
msgid "If you are not sure which category\n"
"your marker can be found under,\n"
"then use this Search tool to find\n"
"the marker you need."
msgstr "如果不确定标记属于哪个类别，\n"
"请使用此搜索工具\n"
"查找所需的标记。"

#: temp.glade:32453
msgid "Find:"
msgstr "查找："

#: temp.glade:32489
msgid "Enable (or disable) the filter to\n"
"only show markers that are in \n"
"use in the current set of books."
msgstr "启用（或禁用）过滤器，\n"
"仅显示当前这组书卷中\n"
"正在使用的标记。"

#: lib/ptxprint/gtkstyleditor.py:722 lib/ptxprint/gtkview.py:2339 temp.glade:32607
msgid "More Info..."
msgstr "更多信息…"

#: temp.glade:32655
msgid "Find a style within the appropriate section which is similar to the new style you wish to create. Then click this Add button to create a new style based on the currently selected style."
msgstr "在相应部分中找到与要创建的新样式相似的样式，然后单击“添加”按钮，即可基于当前所选样式创建新样式。"

#: temp.glade:32702
msgid "Edit"
msgstr "编辑"

#: temp.glade:32706
msgid "Click to Edit additional  \n"
"properties for this style."
msgstr "单击可编辑此样式的\n"
"附加属性。"

#: temp.glade:32808
msgid "Scale Relative \n"
"to Parent"
msgstr "相对于父级\n"
"缩放"

#: temp.glade:32830
msgid "Bold"
msgstr "粗体"

#: temp.glade:32846
msgid "Italic"
msgstr "斜体"

#: temp.glade:32863
msgid "Superscript"
msgstr "上标"

#: temp.glade:32869
msgid "The superscript option overrides these settings:\n"
"   Font Size Factor is set to 0.75\n"
"   Raise is set to 0.85 times the x-height of the font (which\n"
"   defaults to 1/2 the ascent if not specified in the font)."
msgstr "上标选项会覆盖以下设置：\n"
"   字体大小系数设为 0.75\n"
"   上升值设为字体 x 高度的 0.85 倍（\n"
"   如果字体中未指定，则默认为上伸部的 1/2）。"

#: temp.glade:32885
msgid "SmallCaps"
msgstr "小型大写体"

